    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning experiences. They can explain problems in different ways, adapt to a student’s understanding level, and provide instant feedback. They can also offer interactive problem-solving sessions, helping students learn at their own pace. This could reduce anxiety and increase confidence in math, especially for those who struggle with traditional teaching methods."
